### Put a new key
PUT http://localhost:8080/api/v1/kv/hello
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "value": "world"
}

### Get it back
GET http://localhost:8080/api/v1/kv/hello

### Get a key that was never put -> 404
GET http://localhost:8080/api/v1/kv/does-not-exist

### Overwrite an existing key
PUT http://localhost:8080/api/v1/kv/hello
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "value": "world-v2"
}

### Re-get the overwritten key -> should return "world-v2"
GET http://localhost:8080/api/v1/kv/hello

### Put a value over the configured max-value-bytes -> 413
PUT http://localhost:8080/api/v1/kv/too-big
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "value": "replace-this-with-a-string-longer-than-KVSTORE_MAX_VALUE_BYTES-to-see-a-413"
}

### Put with a missing "value" field -> 400
PUT http://localhost:8080/api/v1/kv/invalid
Content-Type: application/json

{}
